  "notes": [
    "Original NanoController binds m_pstrMTextureString to material names containing main and m_pstrMTextureString2 to names containing sub. Bake the static default selection into the native material; keep shaders, samplers, UVs and exact texture payloads.",
    "Swampfire recovery groups have interleaved source indices; ordering is by first occurrence while individual index uniqueness and payload/sibling checks remain strict. Ghostfreak retains the exact case-sensitive Stand1 clip.",
    "Buttercup NpcTexture AssetBundle route points through fileID 1 to Tutorial serialized asset b4f543c102ded400fbc6f1da25d9679a, Texture2D 157. NpcTexture local 157 is mob_queenspider_a and was explicitly rejected.",
    "The original seven repaired models and the three previously missing models are freshly exported from primary using current typed winding/animation contracts. Runty uses the hash-declared native preimage: the sole modification is the exact table-selected main texture, and the complete binary chunk is preserved. Its independent fresh export remains blocked by multiple non-joint renderer transforms; no geometry repair or full Unity visual parity is asserted.",
    "Computress and Runty prefab main materials contain nano_numbuhfour. Primary table and NanoController replace these with nano_computress (Texture2D 487) and nano_runty (488). All 56 applicable production table material bindings were audited.",
    "New overwrite and constant-curve recovery metadata retains clip/target/key/order proofs while omitting legacy asset/pathId lineage. Source publisher checks retain their exact raw identity requirements.",
    "Final native GPU verification of Ghostfreak, Swampfire, Computress and Runty used target/editor-validation/logical_model_gpu_preview.exe linked from current source to avoid the shared Cargo build queue; the normal Cargo replay command is listed above."
  ],
